{"entryId":"3206","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3206:1","sourceSha256":"b663074245006b6d15f75abb317628f5ce1a3b38bc81ef6fd94e9e9e32238f36","englishSha256":"7c1a9cbc4c4d1ef215924de860661852759928abc395e3130f3ba6169bc56672","citations":[{"id":"3206:1:link-001","he":[13,127],"en":[192,200],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_42a.3"},"reference":"Yoma 42a:3","assessment":"Yoma first has Yirmeyah directly address Ravina about the disagreement. It then records the death that day, followed by the mnemonic. The particle כ in the primary mnemonic means “like”; preserve Heilprin’s separate wording where appropriate.","evidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 42a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_42a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3206:1:link-002","he":[129,175],"en":[252,302],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_20b.4"},"reference":"Chullin 20b:4","assessment":"Both the telling direction and the Ravin spelling occur in the checked text.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 20b:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_20b.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3206:1:link-003","he":[177,209],"en":[303,335],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_63a.3"},"reference":"Bava Batra 63a:3","assessment":"The named speaker is directly attested as Ravina bar Kisi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bava Batra 63a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bava_Batra_63a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Yoma directly reports that Yirmeyah spoke to Ravina and then places the death on that day. Hullin and Bava Batra preserve Ravin and Ravina spellings in different passages.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Yoma 42a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Yoma_42a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
